$** | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $15$ | $-13$ | $-5$ | $-4$ | $10$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}$ that best fits the data above can be found using polynomial regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $15$ | $-13$ | $-5$ | $-4$ | $10$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & {0}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 1 & {1}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 2 & {2}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 3 & {3}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{3}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -13 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector."}] [{:db/id 17592186400825 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b2c90d8-0f2e-5f84-bf67-7620d6f1d308" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Design Matrix When the Regression Curve Contains Zero Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "856ff123-4b95-5ec9-8fcf-0c1338ac715a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & (-4)^{2} & (-4)^{3} \\\\ 10 & (-2)^{2} & (-2)^{3} \\\\ -2 & {0}^{2} & {0}^{3} \\\\ 1 & {2}^{2} & {2}^{3} \\\\ 